<article class="env-definition" id="010R">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/010R">Definition <span data-tag="010R">12.12.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}, \mathcal{B}$ be abelian categories. Let $(F^ n, \delta _ F)$ and $(G^ n, \delta _ G)$ be $\delta $-functors from $\mathcal{A}$ to $\mathcal{B}$. A <em>morphism of $\delta $-functors from $F$ to $G$</em> is a collection of transformation of functors $t^ n : F^ n \to G^ n$, $n \geq 0$ such that for every short exact sequence $0 \to A \to B \to C \to 0$ of $\mathcal{A}$ the diagrams </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ F^ n(C) \ar[d]_{t^ n} \ar[rr]_{\delta _{F, A \to B \to C}} &  &  F^{n + 1}(A) \ar[d]^{t^{n + 1}} \\  G^ n(C) \ar[rr]^{\delta _{G, A \to B \to C}} &  &  G^{n + 1}(A) }  \]
</div>
  <p> are commutative. </p>
</article>